## GROWTH tag

Mirrors **`.claude/rules/growth-required.md`**. Keep both files aligned when
editing (per **`.cursor/rules/cursor-claude-doc-sync.mdc`**).

`GROWTH` is a **project-specific** documentation tag (it is *not* one of the
canonical escalation tags in `docs/ai-context.md` — `DESIGN-GAP` /
`DESIGN-FLAW` / `CODE-DEFECT`). It records a **durable, conditional upgrade
path**: the **v0 design is correct until a stated issue or limitation
appears**, then the design **must be amended** to the named option — not
implemented silently in code alone.

### When to use it

Use `GROWTH` when **all** of the following hold:

- **v0 is specified and implementable now** (unlike `DESIGN-GAP`, which blocks),
- A **measurable trigger, scale limit, or operational issue** is named that
  would force a **design change** (architecture, on-disk layout, algorithm tier),
- An **upgrade option** is named (what the design becomes after amendment),
- The tag should **persist** until the trigger fires and the upgrade lands (or
  the trigger is disproven and the tag is removed with evidence).

### How it differs from other tags

| Tag | Meaning | Lifetime |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `DESIGN-GAP` | Not specified yet — **stop, do not guess** | until specified |
| `DESIGN-FLAW` | Design assumption proven wrong — amend now | until amended |
| `CODE-DEFECT` | Code fails a **correct** design — fix code | transient |
| `REWORK-REQUIRED` | Settled design; **code/doc deviates** today | until rework ships |
| **`GROWTH`** | Settled **v0**; **design must change** when trigger/limit hits | until upgrade ships or tag retired with evidence |
| `REFINEMENT` | Deferred detail; v0 path still clear | until refined |

`GROWTH` = "ship v0 as written; when *this* limit bites, amend the design to
*that* upgrade — track it so we do not pretend v0 scales forever."

### Format

- Block form (preferred):

  ```markdown
  > <span class="design-doc-growth">GROWTH GR-Xn</span> — **Trigger:** …
  > **Limitation:** … **Upgrade:** … **v0 until triggered:** …
  ```

- Inline form: `<span class="design-doc-growth">GROWTH</span>`.
- Id convention: `GR-<AREA-LETTER><n>` scoped to the owning doc
  (`GR-S1` in `@PROJ-<AREA>-<n>`, …). Reuse the same id from trade studies or
  cross-doc restatements.
- **Reservation:** allocate **`GR-…`** only via **`tasks/TAG-REGISTRY.md`**
  (**commit and push** before use) — **`.cursor/rules/tag-reservation.mdc`**.

CSS class `design-doc-growth` (teal) lives in
`docs/stylesheets/labzero-extra.css`, parallel to `design-doc-refine`,
`design-doc-gap`, and `design-doc-rework`.

### Discipline

- Do **not** implement the upgrade path in code while v0 is still authoritative
  unless the trigger has been measured and the design amended in the same change.
- When the trigger fires: amend design per `docs/ai-context.md`, implement,
  **remove** the `GROWTH` tag (or replace with a short "resolved" note in the
  amendment block).
- Every tag must state **trigger**, **limitation**, **upgrade**, and **v0**
  so it is actionable cold.
- Surface `GROWTH` tags in handoffs and ticket planning like `REWORK-REQUIRED`.

### Runtime monitoring (evaluable triggers)

When a **`GR-…`** trigger is **objectively measurable** at runtime, implement
optional monitoring and **`GROWTH_TRIGGERED`** logging per
**`.cursor/rules/growth-monitoring.mdc`** (mirrored **`.claude/rules/growth-monitoring.md`**).
Monitors must be **compile-outable** and **runtime-disableable** so v0 stays
efficient. Add a **`Monitor:`** line to the design block when evaluable.
